{"id":"overtime-by-unit","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"Overtime and other pay by bargaining unit","question":"In fiscal 2026, which bargaining units were paid the most overtime and other pay, against their regular pay, and how fast has it grown?","finding":"In fiscal 2026 the City paid $513.4 million in overtime and $283.9 million in other pay on $4.92 billion of regular pay. Five units drew 70.7% of the overtime: POA (unit 911) $156.8 million (47.1% of its regular pay, 70,190 dollars per person paid); Firefighters,Local 798, Unit 1 (unit 798) $63.9 million (23.8% of its regular pay, 34,097 dollars per person paid); SEIU, Local 1021, Misc (unit 790) $53.1 million (6.1% of its regular pay, 4,776 dollars per person paid); Deputy Sheriffs' Assoc (DSA) (unit 498) $47.8 million (50.0% of its regular pay, 63,366 dollars per person paid); TWU, Local 250-A, TransitOpr (unit 253) $41.2 million (20.6% of its regular pay, 16,239 dollars per person paid). Among units with $5 million or more of overtime, the fastest growth since fiscal 2019 was Sheriffs' Mgrs and Supv (MSA) (unit 499) (2.65 times) and POA (unit 911) (2.57 times).","how":"Every fiscal-year row of the Controller's Employee Compensation file is summed by the union code the file gives it (one bargaining unit), and named as the file names it. People paid are distinct names with pay in the unit that year. Overtime share is overtime divided by salaries (regular pay). Growth is the latest year's overtime divided by the same unit's overtime in fiscal 2019 and 2014, shown only where the earlier year had $100,000 or more. 'Overtime above salary' counts rows with a salary of $40,000 or more and more overtime than salary. The citywide totals match the overtime table already on this site ($513.4 million in fiscal 2026).","limits":"Overtime follows vacancies, minimum staffing set in labor agreements, 24-hour fire shifts, and outside events billed to others; it is a question about staffing and control, not proof that any hour was not worked. Other pay holds premiums, retention pay, leave cash-outs at retirement and lump sums the labor agreements set; most of it is set by contract. A unit's code can change or split between years, so growth for a unit that was renumbered can look large or be missing. A person who changed units counts in both.","columns":[{"k":"unit","t":"Union (bargaining unit)","type":"text"},{"k":"employees","t":"People paid","type":"int"},{"k":"regular","t":"Regular pay","type":"usd"},{"k":"overtime","t":"Overtime","type":"usd"},{"k":"otShare","t":"Overtime / regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"otPer","t":"Overtime per person","type":"usd"},{"k":"other","t":"Other pay","type":"usd"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Other pay / regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"otGrowth19","t":"Overtime vs 2019","type":"times"},{"k":"otGrowth14","t":"Overtime vs 2014","type":"times"},{"k":"otherGrowth19","t":"Other pay vs 2019","type":"times"},{"k":"otOverSalary","t":"Overtime above salary (rows)","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"unit":"POA (unit 911)","employees":2234,"regular":333145839,"overtime":156805066,"otShare":0.4707,"otPer":70190,"other":58095427,"otherShare":0.1744,"otGrowth19":2.5746,"otGrowth14":5.657,"otherGrowth19":3.0285,"otOverSalary":203},{"unit":"Firefighters,Local 798, Unit 1 (unit 798)","employees":1873,"regular":268708419,"overtime":63864170,"otShare":0.2377,"otPer":34097,"other":45463220,"otherShare":0.1692,"otGrowth19":1.7038,"otGrowth14":1.5647,"otherGrowth19":1.7396,"otOverSalary":29},{"unit":"SEIU, Local 1021, Misc (unit 790)","employees":11115,"regular":868572874,"overtime":53086661,"otShare":0.0611,"otPer":4776,"other":25102648,"otherShare":0.0289,"otGrowth19":1.5319,"otGrowth14":3.2409,"otherGrowth19":1.5113,"otOverSalary":35},{"unit":"Deputy Sheriffs' Assoc (DSA) (unit 498)","employees":755,"regular":95606371,"overtime":47841098,"otShare":0.5004,"otPer":63366,"other":10657698,"otherShare":0.1115,"otGrowth19":1.8734,"otGrowth14":5.1717,"otherGrowth19":1.4229,"otOverSalary":83},{"unit"